---
number: 54
title: Great, Thou Jehovah
author: Anonymous
composer: Lajos Kovacz
sp_category: "5"
topic: God’s Majesty
---

[verse 1]
Great, Thou Jehovah, is Thy mighty power,
Creating life, by Thy divine command;
Order from chaos came when Thou hadst spoken;
Light, life, and beauty on both sea and land.
The myriad stars, the sun in golden glory,
Everything by Thy summons came to be;
My heart is bowed in awe and adoration,
All of creation sings its praise to Thee.

[verse 2]
Great, Thou Jehovah, is Thy matchless wisdom,
Beauty and order are creation’s goal;
To man Thou gavest sonship in Thy kingdom;
From Thine own spirit came his living soul.
Whether in grass or in the mighty oak tree,
Signs of Thy hand my eyes can clearly trace;
With open hearted reverence and meekness,
Thy glorious wisdom I will gladly praise.

[verse 3]
Great, Thou Jehovah, is Thy boundless mercy;
In Christ Thy Son my heart can know Thy care;
Thou wilt accept that flame within me burning;
This bruised reed in mercy Thou wilt spare.
Once bound in evil, captive in its fetters,
Thou didst deliver by Thy mighty hand;
With tears of joy, on bended knee, I bless Thee
For that dear love in which I now can stand.
